<doc id="180722" url="https://jv.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=180722" title="Kintetsu Department Store">
Kintetsu Department Store

Kintetsu Department Store Co., Ltd. (株式会社近鉄百貨店, Kabushiki gaisha Kintetsu Hyakkaten) yaiku jaringan &lt;a href="department%20store%20ing%20Jepang"&gt;department store&lt;/a&gt; ing wilayah &lt;a href="Kansai"&gt;Kansai&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="Jepang"&gt;Jepang&lt;/a&gt;.
Kantor pusaté ing Abenosuji Itchome, &lt;a href="Abeno-ku%2C%20Osaka"&gt;Abeno-ku&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="Osaka"&gt;Osaka&lt;/a&gt;, Jepang.
<h2>Sajarah</h2>
<ul>
<li>Januari 1920: Kyoto Bussankan (京都物産館, Kyoto Bussankan) dibukak ing ngarepe Stasiun Kyoto.</li>
<li>Februari 1920: Kyoto Bussankan General Partnership (合名会社京都物産館, Kyoto Bussankan General Partnership) didegaké.</li>
<li>1926: Osaka Electric Railway Co., Ltd. (大阪電気軌道株式会社, Osaka Electric Railway Co., Ltd. sadurunge saka Kintetsu Corporation) mbukak restoran dhewe ing Daiki Building ing Uehommachi, Osaka.</li>
<li>1930: Kyoto Bussankan General Partnership mbukak gerai cabang ing Yanagase, Gifu.</li>
<li>September 1931: Kyoto Bussankan General Partnership diganti jeneng dadi Marubutsu General Partnership (合名会社丸物, Marubutsu General Partnership).</li>
<li>29 September 1934: Marubutsu General Partnership direorganisasi dadi Marubutsu Company (株式会社丸物, Marubutsu Company).</li>
<li>1934: Osaka Railway Co., Ltd. (大阪鉄道株式会社, Osaka Railway Co., Ltd.) didegaké Daitetsu Department Store Company (株式会社大鉄百貨店, Daitetsu Department Store Company).</li>
<li>September 1936: Daiki Department Store (大軌百貨店, Daiki Department Store) dibukak ing Uehommachi, Osaka.</li>
<li>November 1937: Daitetsu Department Store dibukak ing Abeno, Osaka.</li>
<li>Maret 1941: Daiki nggabungake Sangu Kyuko Railway Company lan diganti jeneng Kansai Kyuko Electric Railway Co., Ltd. (関西急行鉄道株式会社, Kansai Kyuko Electric Railway Co., Ltd.), mangkono, Daiki Department Store diganti jeneng Kankyu Department Store (関急百貨店, Kankyu Department Store).</li>
<li>1 April 1944: Kankyu nggabungake Daitetsu Department Store Company, mula, Kankyu Department Store dibangun maneh dadi Kankyu Department Store Uehommachi (関急百貨店上本町店, Kankyu Department Store Uehommachi) lan Daitetsu Department Store (大鉄百貨店, Daitetsu Department Store) dadi Kankyu Department Store Abeno (関急百貨店阿倍野店, Kankyu Department Store Abeno).</li>
<li>1 Juni 1944: Kankyu lan Nankai Railway padha digabungake kanggo mbentuk Kinki Nippon Railway Co., Ltd. (近畿日本鉄道株式会社, Kinki Nippon Railway Co., Ltd. Kinki Nippon utawa Kin-Nichi, saiki: Kintetsu Group Holdings Co., Ltd.). Kankyu Department Stores diganti jeneng Kinki Nippon Railway Uehommachi Department Store (近畿日本鉄道上本町百貨店, Kinki Nippon Railway Uehommachi Department Store) lan Kinki Nippon Railway Abeno Department Store (近畿日本鉄道阿倍野百貨店, Kinki Nippon Railway Abeno Department Store).</li>
<li>1948: Kinki Nippon Railway Department Stores diganti jeneng Kintetsu Department Store Uehommachi (近鉄百貨店上本町店, Kintetsu Department Store Uehommachi) lan Kintetsu Department Store Abeno (近鉄百貨店阿倍野店, Kintetsu Department Store Abeno).</li>
